# Worker settings (apps/worker; see its README and docs/install.md). With LAUNCHPAD_DEPLOYMENTS
# unset or off, the worker reads nothing else, opens no database and needs no Dokku credentials; it
# only keeps a health marker (LAUNCHPAD_WORKER_HEALTH_FILE, if your supervisor checks one).
#
# To enable deployments, set the same value on the controller and the worker, then restart both:
# LAUNCHPAD_DEPLOYMENTS=on
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...                 # the controller's database
# LAUNCHPAD_DATA_DIR=/data                    # the controller's shared archive volume
# LAUNCHPAD_BASE_URL=https://controller.example
# LAUNCHPAD_APPS_DOMAIN=sites.example.net
# LAUNCHPAD_APPS_PROXY_URL=http://dokku:80    # the Dokku proxy as the worker reaches it
# DOKKU_SSH_HOST=dokku
# DOKKU_SSH_PORT=22
# DOKKU_SSH_USER=dokku
# DOKKU_SSH_KEY_PATH=/credentials/id_ed25519  # mount read-only
# DOKKU_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS_PATH=/credentials/known_hosts
# LAUNCHPAD_BASE_IMAGE=nginx:1.27-alpine      # pin by digest for a release
# LAUNCHPAD_WORKER_HEALTH_FILE=/tmp/launchpad-worker-health
